DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These routines return a string of characters in _s_t_r,  starting  at  the
       current  cursor  position in the named window.  Attributes are stripped
       from the characters.

       The four functions with _n as the last argument return  a  leading  sub‐
       string  at  most  _n  characters  long  (exclusive of the trailing NUL).
       Transfer stops at the end of the current line,  or  when  _n  characters
       have been stored at the location referenced by _s_t_r.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       All  of the functions return EERRRR upon failure, or the number of charac‐
       ters actually read into the string.

       X/Open Curses defines no error conditions.  This implementation returns
       an error

       •   if the _w_i_n parameter is null or

       •   if the _c_h_s_t_r parameter is null.

       Functions  prefixed with “mv” first perform cursor movement and fail if
       the position (_y, _x) is outside the window boundaries.

